WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
I am going to the live hacking event.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.040
Having so many talented hunters there,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.560
I need to do my best and maybe even more.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.600
I found a bug on literally the first day of hacking.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.879
Closed as informative.

00:00:17.959 --> 00:00:19.840
I'm not finding anything.

00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:24.080
Worst time of my professional career.

00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:29.320
Aligned perfectly for a really, really nice bug.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.480
$10,000.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.799
This bug is even better than $13,000.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.720
Total of _ thousand dollars.

00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:52.919
I have just learned that I will be going to my first live hacking event.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:56.400
I just got the email of the invitation to H1702

00:00:56.799 --> 00:00:59.360
in Vegas, close to DEFCON.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.400
I have no idea who the customer is.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.799
I have no idea about pretty much nothing yet.

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:07.040
Right now, it's 20th May, 2024.

00:01:07.559 --> 00:01:08.440
I'm in Barcelona.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.639
I just got the news.

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:11.120
I am super, super happy.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.519
It was one of my dreams to get to a live hacking event.

00:01:15.199 --> 00:01:17.639
And I didn't expect this one as well.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.480
I know I've been plus oned by Justin for the event in January,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.239
and then I kind of expected the invitation.

00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.559
And I was quite, quite sad I didn't get it.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.919
Now, I knew there was a possibility I will be going to DEFCON,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.480
but the live hacking event I didn't really think a lot about.

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:39.199
But I got the invitation.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.440
I am incredibly, incredibly happy.

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:47.199
And I just, you know, randomly decided to spontaneously record this video.

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:50.760
And I'll probably record the whole journey, the whole...

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.919
I don't know. I have no idea yet.

00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:56.440
But if you're watching this, it means that I have come up

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.080
with a good plan on what to record, and I have recorded it already.

00:02:00.599 --> 00:02:04.839
So without further ado, I won't hold you up here for longer.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:06.599
Enjoy the video.

00:02:15.279 --> 00:02:18.399
It is time for the first live hacking event update.

00:02:18.759 --> 00:02:22.360
It's 27th June, so there's still three more weeks

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.520
until the start of the virtual phase of the event.

00:02:26.039 --> 00:02:29.919
But Alex Chapman in the interview gave me a really good tip

00:02:29.919 --> 00:02:33.759
to start hacking on the target as soon as we know the customers.

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.399
And we do know the customers already.

00:02:36.399 --> 00:02:40.399
These are, I hope I can say, if not, I will bleep, TikTok and Epic Games.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.839
And these targets are I've never hacked on before.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.800
So I really, really want to use the time before.

00:02:48.559 --> 00:02:51.839
I already have like started a little bit.

00:02:51.839 --> 00:02:54.600
I just created Bear Projects and Kaido Projects.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.559
I created my setup and nothing more.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.080
But I really do want to get advantage of starting a little bit earlier

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.919
to do some recon, because I do feel some pressure, to be honest,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.279
to perform at this event.

00:03:07.279 --> 00:03:11.119
You know, just thinking about having so many talented hunters there

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:16.240
does make me feel that I need to do my best and maybe even more

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.399
to do well at the event.

00:03:18.399 --> 00:03:20.440
To be honest, I quite like it,

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.960
because normally there's not much pressure in bug bounty.

00:03:24.039 --> 00:03:28.360
You know, you don't directly compete with other people.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.759
I am my hacking style.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.240
I rarely find duplicates, duplicates.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.000
So I do really like the push to perform at my best.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.639
I'm motivated to do very meticulous nodes.

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:45.000
I already created my my setup with two proxies.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.160
I proxy the traffic. Kaido will be my main proxy.

00:03:48.839 --> 00:03:53.000
But in front of Kaido, I use Burp to be able to use Burp browser

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.679
because I like DomInvader and to also use some some passive Burp plugins.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.600
I hope the performance will not

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.800
will not be too bad with the setup, but we'll see.

00:04:06.639 --> 00:04:10.600
Also, I want to try the JS Weasel tool for the event.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.360
It is a tool for working with JavaScript files and it's a commercial tool.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:19.000
But I asked and they offered to extend my trial

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.160
for the period of the whole event.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.320
So a huge thanks for them and a shout out.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.839
You can check out the JS Weasel using the link from the description.

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:34.640
And also, I'm quite puzzled as to what new things should I add to my

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.279
to my hacking style, because I recorded two podcasts recently,

00:04:38.279 --> 00:04:43.000
one with Alex Chapman, who who spoke about testing desktop applications

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.320
and the other one with Joel with TechnoGeek.

00:04:46.799 --> 00:04:50.160
And he's a very good mobile app tester.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.760
And one of these targets has a lot of mobile apps,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.480
has like four or five different mobile apps in scope.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.480
The other target has a lot of desktop apps.

00:05:00.079 --> 00:05:04.519
And I don't know if I should, you know, invest the time now into learning

00:05:04.959 --> 00:05:08.160
about, you know, basically spending time learning something

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.399
almost completely new to me,

00:05:10.399 --> 00:05:15.760
or I should just stick to what I know and to what I already can do well.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.720
I don't know. I will see.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.720
I will record an update at some point in the future.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.399
So you will see it in a few minutes.

00:05:23.519 --> 00:05:27.959
For now, for me at least, it is a mystery of what will happen.

00:05:28.279 --> 00:05:30.839
But I am very, very excited.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:45.679
So we are in between the virtual phase of the live hacking event

00:05:45.679 --> 00:05:48.119
and the in-person phase.

00:05:48.119 --> 00:05:50.040
I fly to Las Vegas tomorrow.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.200
It is 3rd August.

00:05:54.079 --> 00:05:57.480
And the virtual phase was a real rollercoaster for me.

00:05:58.239 --> 00:06:01.399
It started quite well, at least I thought it does.

00:06:01.399 --> 00:06:04.160
I found a bug on literally the first day of hacking.

00:06:05.239 --> 00:06:09.160
And I was happy about it because it was my biggest worry

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.119
that I would end up the whole event with with no bugs.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.160
I submitted the bug.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.559
Unfortunately, it was closed as informative,

00:06:16.679 --> 00:06:19.799
which I could make an argument against it.

00:06:19.799 --> 00:06:23.119
Maybe I will collaborate with somebody because I think there is a potential

00:06:23.119 --> 00:06:27.239
that somebody knows better how to show the impact of this.

00:06:27.559 --> 00:06:31.320
For now, I can't really be upset about this one.

00:06:32.119 --> 00:06:33.640
So I continued hacking.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.320
I submitted another bug.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.959
Unfortunately, it was also closed as informative,

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.279
which I wasn't particularly happy about it.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.519
This one, I don't really agree with.

00:06:42.519 --> 00:06:46.559
I think the attack scenario that I was able to show should be good enough

00:06:46.559 --> 00:06:50.079
to trigger this as a medium and maybe as a low.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.760
But the program decided otherwise can't really do much about it.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:59.959
So I just kept on hacking, but I was finding no bugs.

00:06:59.959 --> 00:07:05.079
And the worst part about it was that I was finding very interesting targets,

00:07:05.079 --> 00:07:08.559
interesting functionalities where I was like, oh, one hundred percent.

00:07:08.559 --> 00:07:10.279
There are bugs in this functionality.

00:07:10.279 --> 00:07:12.320
This is too complex to be secure.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.880
But the problem was that

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.320
nothing worked like literally nothing.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.320
I tried worked.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.679
And in some cases, I saw the error message

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.519
and the error message basically told me that, you know,

00:07:28.799 --> 00:07:31.799
this there has been an attack here, but we fixed it.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.799
Sometimes you just feel that the functionality you're testing

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:42.239
has been vulnerable before, but somebody else got the bounty for it.

00:07:42.239 --> 00:07:44.720
And I felt like this here.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:49.040
And at this point, you also have the Slack channel for all participants

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.040
where people can ask for collaborations,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.320
people can ask questions to programs, people can post memes.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.000
And in general, I saw that

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.040
first, not a lot of people were finding bugs.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.839
People had problems finding bugs.

00:08:04.839 --> 00:08:06.880
So I felt a little bit better.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.359
That is not only me struggling at this point.

00:08:10.079 --> 00:08:13.200
The other thing that I noticed was also people

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.279
are referencing past life hacking events of the same customers.

00:08:18.359 --> 00:08:22.079
And this one was a little bit problematic for me because

00:08:24.279 --> 00:08:28.160
in conjunction also with a lot of people asking questions about the targets,

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.440
I just called interesting.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:36.080
So I was like, OK, a lot of hunters are hunting on the same target as I am.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.559
And even worse, they already have the experience from these targets,

00:08:40.559 --> 00:08:42.440
from past life hacking events.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.280
And because these targets were part of past hacking events,

00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:48.559
they are also quite hardened.

00:08:49.599 --> 00:08:52.359
And then they published the leaderboard.

00:08:52.359 --> 00:08:55.640
And I saw that at first there weren't many bugs.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.200
But then I saw, you know, people people do find stuff.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:03.320
And at this point, I started feeling horrible,

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:08.359
like about one and a half week out of the two week virtual phase.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:14.559
It was the worst time of my professional career,

00:09:14.559 --> 00:09:18.359
like I've never felt so bad because of my work, because I felt

00:09:19.039 --> 00:09:21.320
like I'm not finding anything.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:24.200
And one week ago, if you asked me,

00:09:24.359 --> 00:09:29.559
I would say I'm almost sure I will end up the event with no valid bugs.

00:09:30.119 --> 00:09:36.719
I even planned initially to record the part of this vlog during the event.

00:09:37.679 --> 00:09:42.599
But then I was like, if I don't find bugs, there's no point publishing this video.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.159
So I didn't record anything during this phase.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.799
I felt horrible. I didn't want to hack.

00:09:49.799 --> 00:09:52.039
I sort of just wanted it to be over.

00:09:53.039 --> 00:09:56.599
But then the next week, I just kept on hacking.

00:09:56.599 --> 00:10:01.679
I also listened to the podcast, listened to advice from my own podcast,

00:10:01.679 --> 00:10:03.799
from one of the recent episodes.

00:10:03.799 --> 00:10:05.960
And I did find a really interesting target.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:09.719
And all of a sudden, everything clicked like my exploit.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:16.440
All the pieces of the exploit aligned perfectly for a really, really nice bug,

00:10:17.479 --> 00:10:20.520
which took me like one and a half days to exploit.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.520
But it is a really nice bug.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:28.000
I hope I will get the permission to to create a video about this bug.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.200
But for now, I cannot disclose any details.

00:10:31.919 --> 00:10:35.960
Unfortunately, it is a duplicate, but because it's a duplicate window,

00:10:36.559 --> 00:10:38.200
I will get half of the bounty.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.520
So it doesn't, bounty wise, it doesn't matter if you're the first

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.840
or the second person reporting the bug in the in the window.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.679
You still get get your piece of the bounty.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:55.919
So this is this is the one that the original report is still in the new phase.

00:10:55.919 --> 00:11:00.080
So I don't know what will be the risk, but I don't think it will be lower than high.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:04.400
I think it's either high or critical because I was able to show a lot of impact.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.840
So I'm really, really happy about this one.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.200
And finally, it was on Epic Games.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:14.919
And as you know, from the from the previous part I recorded,

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.239
I spent some time before the event.

00:11:18.239 --> 00:11:22.200
But the funny thing is, I spent all the time before the event on TikTok

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:27.880
and then during the event up until the last day, I only hacked on Epic Games.

00:11:28.679 --> 00:11:32.080
And I don't know why, to be honest, don't ask me.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.280
I don't know why it just happened to be this way.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.679
But even on the last day of the virtual event,

00:11:40.599 --> 00:11:43.919
I got an email from TikTok about a new functionality

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.960
in the in the application.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:52.320
And I noticed that I only got this email to my real account,

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:58.359
to my real Bug Bounty Report Explained account that has real videos, real followers.

00:11:59.039 --> 00:12:01.280
I also maybe this is the important bit.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.159
I also actually purchased ads in the past.

00:12:05.239 --> 00:12:08.719
And maybe that's why I got the email to this account

00:12:08.719 --> 00:12:11.159
and to none of my testing accounts.

00:12:12.159 --> 00:12:17.719
And I thought, you know, OK, if they just launched a new product now

00:12:18.719 --> 00:12:23.440
and possibly other hunters did not receive an update about this,

00:12:23.559 --> 00:12:25.200
I should probably look there.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.039
In like less than one hour, I found a bug.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.359
It is a medium. I reported it as a medium.

00:12:30.359 --> 00:12:34.039
It's not a super critical bug, but you might say just a medium.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.320
Mediums during these live hacking events are paid a lot on TikTok.

00:12:38.359 --> 00:12:42.400
A medium gives you the range of $2,000 to $9,000.

00:12:42.599 --> 00:12:44.960
You can get $9,000 for a medium.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:48.400
On Epic, it is, I think, $3,000 to $7,000.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.840
So this bug, it was on TikTok.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.520
It went through the pre-triage.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.880
It is in the pending program review state, which means it is not a duplicate.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.359
So I'm really happy about it.

00:13:01.359 --> 00:13:02.880
I hope it will be triaged.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.559
I hope TikTok will not come up with some strange

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:09.159
reason why it wouldn't be.

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.200
Then I also found another one.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.840
This one, the CVSS said it's high,

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.559
in which it actually is.

00:13:17.559 --> 00:13:19.919
The problem is it is sort of on the edge of the scope.

00:13:20.479 --> 00:13:26.000
I do hope it will be triaged, but it may as well not be.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:30.559
So these are the three reports that I reported during the virtual phase.

00:13:30.559 --> 00:13:35.599
And I'm still waiting for updates on all of them, to be honest.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.880
But then in this between phase,

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:45.119
I also collaborated with another hacker, with Jonathan Baumel.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:49.760
And the same bug that I reported, I told you, is really nice.

00:13:50.679 --> 00:13:54.799
We found another way to get to the same, to achieve the same impact.

00:13:54.799 --> 00:13:58.000
Basically, part of the exploit is shared between these two.

00:13:58.919 --> 00:14:00.799
But it is a new bug.

00:14:00.799 --> 00:14:05.359
And this bug is even better than the one I submitted myself.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:10.799
So, again, I really hope I will be able to make a video about this.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:16.880
But this bug we will submit tomorrow once the window reopens.

00:14:17.679 --> 00:14:22.479
And I hope that nobody has, because the way these things work

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.359
is there is a dupe window that lasts two weeks.

00:14:26.359 --> 00:14:30.599
So if many people submit the same bug within these two weeks,

00:14:30.799 --> 00:14:33.400
the reward will be split between all of them.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.760
Then there is a pause and then there's another dupe window.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.119
And that another dupe window is when we submit the bug.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:43.960
But if it turns out that somebody has already reported this bug

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.880
in the previous dupe window, we will not be splitting the bounty.

00:14:47.719 --> 00:14:49.760
So let's hope this is not the case.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.960
I would be really heartbroken.

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.080
But it is what it is.

00:14:54.239 --> 00:14:57.359
So I have four reports at the moment that I'm still waiting

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.159
for them to be processed.

00:15:00.159 --> 00:15:03.960
I'm fairly happy with my performance here.

00:15:04.479 --> 00:15:07.840
I hope that the rewards for this will be

00:15:09.039 --> 00:15:10.960
what I expect them to be.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.559
Then I will be really, really happy with this life hacking event.

00:15:13.559 --> 00:15:18.080
But to be honest, for me, the biggest goal of this life hacking event

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:22.000
is not measured in the number of reports, is not measured

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.479
in the amount of bounty I received.

00:15:24.479 --> 00:15:29.000
I received it is measured in whether I will get to

00:15:30.239 --> 00:15:32.919
receive invitations for future life hacking events,

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.880
because the goal for me is

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:39.440
for this event is to show my hacking skills

00:15:40.359 --> 00:15:43.840
so that I just get to the life hacking event circle

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.679
like keep getting these these invitations to these events.

00:15:46.679 --> 00:15:48.880
It will be awesome for me.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:52.159
It would be really nice to just be able to be part of this.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.799
So I hope that that these bugs will get

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.880
processed well, will get good bounties.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:04.679
Maybe I will even show and tell one of them because Jonathan,

00:16:04.679 --> 00:16:07.479
who has been to many life hacking events,

00:16:07.479 --> 00:16:09.919
so he knows much more about these than me.

00:16:11.359 --> 00:16:14.719
He told me that this bug is a show and tell material.

00:16:14.719 --> 00:16:19.359
So maybe we could get to to show this back on the stage in Vegas

00:16:19.359 --> 00:16:20.960
in front of everyone.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:24.919
It would be it would be mind blowing and an awesome opportunity.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:28.520
So let's let's see what happens.

00:16:28.919 --> 00:16:34.559
Probably the next time I talk with you will be after the event from from Vegas.

